CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   [3]  sites; exons only.
CC       For an overview of the musigdjc loci see the first paragraph of
CC   'comment' in musigdjc01.
CC       The mRNA transcript which encodes the c-mu region also encodes
CC   the c-delta region and is subject to a series of alternative
CC   processing pathways. First, the mRNA can be spliced for either the
CC   mu or delta constant heavy chain. Then it can follow two paths
CC   within mu and possibly as many as five within delta (see musigdjc14
CC   regarding the delta pathways). The first c-mu pathway produces the
CC   secreted form of IgM. The secreted tail (the c-terminal
CC   polypeptide) is encoded immediately 3' to the c-mu-4 domain and is
CC   included in this locus. The membrane-bound form is expressed via
CC   the second c-mu pathway: the secreted tail codons are spliced out
CC   and the 3' membrane exons(mu-m1 & mu-m2) are translated. See
CC   musigdjc11 for the membrane exons. Unlike many other c-h genes,
CC   c-mu has 4 coding domains instead of 3 domains and a hinge exon.
CC   Complete source information:
CC   mouse (strain BALB/c) liver([8]), newborn([6],[9]) sperm([2]) DNA;
CC   myeloma hpc76([7]) DNA; myelomas tepc183([3]), mopc 104e([4],[1]),
CC   sp1/hl hybridoma([5]), cDNA to mRNA.
